sccs.csv is the `sccs` example data set of the R package EmpiricalCalibration 3.1.4
(CRAN, Apache License 2.0; Martijn Schuemie and Marc Suchard, OHDSI): 45 negative-control
drugs and one drug of interest (sertraline) with the log rate ratio and its standard error
from a self-controlled case series. It is copied unchanged (data(sccs), written with
write.csv) so that the engine's empirical-null case can be held to the numbers that package
documents in its vignette (null mean 0.7922, SD 0.2834, calibrated p 0.8389) without adding
the package to any locked library. The license text is LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt.

References: Schuemie MJ, Ryan PB, DuMouchel W, Suchard MA, Madigan D. Interpreting
observational studies: why empirical calibration is needed to correct p-values.
Stat Med 2014;33:209-218 (PMID 23900808).
